{
  "id": "mcq-zero-padding",
  "unit": "string-basics",
  "mode": "choice",
  "tier": "medium",
  "title": "Which script produces this output?",
  "topics": [
    "as",
    "format",
    "++"
  ],
  "examObjective": "Applying correct syntax to write DataWeave transformations to coerce, format, order, and filter data",
  "prompt": "Given the payload below, **which script produces exactly this output?**\n\n```\n\"ORD-0012\"\n```",
  "inputMime": "application/json",
  "outputMime": "application/json",
  "choice": {
    "kind": "which-script",
    "payload": "{\"n\":12}",
    "target": "\"ORD-0012\"",
    "answer": 3,
    "options": [
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n\"ORD-$(payload.n)\"",
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n\"ORD-\" ++ (payload.n as String {format: \"####\"})",
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n\"ORD-00\" + payload.n",
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n\"ORD-\" ++ (payload.n as String {format: \"0000\"})"
    ]
  },
  "cases": [],
  "solution": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n\"ORD-\" ++ (payload.n as String {format: \"0000\"})",
  "explanation": {
    "approach": "In a number pattern, `0` is a digit that is always printed and `#` is one that is dropped when it would be a leading zero. Padding needs zeros.",
    "snippets": [
      {
        "label": "The answer",
        "script": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n\"ORD-\" ++ (payload.n as String {format: \"0000\"})",
        "payload": "{\"n\":12}",
        "expect": {
          "output": "\"ORD-0012\""
        },
        "note": "Four mandatory digits."
      },
      {
        "label": "Interpolation keeps the number as it is",
        "script": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n\"ORD-$(payload.n)\"",
        "payload": "{\"n\":12}",
        "expect": {
          "output": "\"ORD-12\""
        },
        "note": "No padding happens without a format."
      },
      {
        "label": "Hashes are optional digits",
        "script": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n\"ORD-\" ++ (payload.n as String {format: \"####\"})",
        "payload": "{\"n\":12}",
        "expect": {
          "output": "\"ORD-12\""
        },
        "note": "The leading positions are left out."
      },
      {
        "label": "+ tries arithmetic",
        "script": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n\"ORD-00\" + payload.n",
        "payload": "{\"n\":12}",
        "expect": {
          "error": true
        },
        "note": "\"ORD-00\" is not a number, so `+` has nothing to add."
      }
    ]
  }
}
